Father-Canon Jean Mignon, played by Murray Melvin.

12
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:46,000
The Devils is a 1971 historical psychological horror-drama film written, produced and
directed by Ken Russell, and starring Vanessa Redgrave and Oliver Reed.

13
00:54:53,333 --> 00:54:59,333
A dramatised historical account of the fall of Urbain Grandier, a 17th-century Roman Catholic priest accused of witchcraft after the
possessions in Loudun, France, the plot also focuses on Sister Jeanne des Anges, a sexually repressed nun who incites the accusations.

14
00:59:06,666 --> 00:59:12,666
A co-production between the United Kingdom and the United States, The Devils is in part adapted from the 1952 non-fiction
book The Devils of Loudun by Aldous Huxley, as well as John Whiting's subsequent 1960 play The Devils.

15
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
United Artists initially pitched the idea to Russell but bowed out after reading his
finished screenplay, as they felt it was too controversial in nature.

16
01:07:33,333 --> 01:07:39,333
Warner Bros.

17
01:11:46,666 --> 01:11:52,666
agreed to produce and distribute, and filming largely took
place at Pinewood Studios in late 1970.

18
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film's graphic portrayal of violent and sexual content, often combined with religion, ignited harsh reaction
from censors, and it originally received an X rating in both the United Kingdom and the United States.

19
01:20:13,333 --> 01:20:19,333
It was banned in several countries, and heavily edited for exhibition in others.

20
01:24:26,666 --> 01:24:32,666
Although critics largely dismissed the film for its explicit content, it won awards for Best
Director at the 33rd Venice International Film Festival, as well as from the U.S.

21
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
National Board of Review.

22
01:32:53,333 --> 01:32:59,333
Although a restoration of Russell's director's cut of The Devils was given its first theatrical release in the UK in 2002, this version has not
been made officially available on home media, and releases of edited versions of the film on DVD and streaming services remain scant.

23
01:37:06,666 --> 01:37:12,666
Film scholarship primarily focuses on themes of sexual
repression and political corruption.

24
01:41:20,000 --> 01:41:26,000
The Devils has been recognized as one of the most controversial films of all time by
numerous publications and critics, and remained banned in Finland until 2001.

25
01:45:33,333 --> 01:45:39,333
The film explores themes of nun, chaos, christianity, inquisition, exploitation.

26
01:49:46,666 --> 01:49:52,666
The tone is dark and emotional and mind_bending.
